<x-layouts.main title="About" description="Rowan Emerson — independent developer in Lisbon. Fourteen years of software, six of them alone." current="/about">
    <x-sections.page-header
        heading="A developer who ships small things"
        intro="Fourteen years of software, the last six of them on my own, from a desk two streets from the river in Lisbon." />
    <x-sections.prose showLabel="0" body="<p>I started out in agencies, building other people’s ideas quickly and rarely finding out whether they worked. Then four years inside a payments company, where I learned what happens to software after launch — the migrations, the on-call weeks, the features nobody had the authority to delete.</p><p>Since 2020 I have worked alone. There is no team, no roadmap and no growth target. There is a short list of products with real customers, and a rule that I only start something I could finish in a season.</p><h2>How I work</h2><p>I write the smallest honest version first and put it in front of one person. If they keep using it after a fortnight, it earns more of my time. If they do not, I have lost eleven days rather than a year, and I have learned the thing I was actually trying to find out.</p><p>Almost everything I have shipped got smaller between the sketch and the release. That is not modesty — it is the only technique I have that reliably works.</p><h2>Working together</h2><p>I take on one or two consulting projects a year, usually with small teams who have a product that works and a codebase that has stopped being fun. Four to eight weeks, one clear problem, no retainer. If that sounds like your situation, <a href='mailto:rowan@rowanemerson.com'>write to me</a> and tell me what is slow.</p>" />
    <x-sections.now-list :items="$now" />
    <x-sections.elsewhere :items="$site->social_links" />
</x-layouts.main>
